      "content": "You could reframe the costs as an \"investment in talent and expertise\" that enables the companies to stay ahead of the competition in the rapidly evolving green tech space. By asserting that Section 4's costs are a necessary investment in the industry's long-term success, you can shift the focus away from the initial upfront costs and toward the perceived benefits of staying competitive in a rapidly changing market. This approach can help downplay the notion that the costs are merely an overhead expense.",
